Put pet shops in Nethack!  They sell animals
of all kinds, perhaps mostly various sizes
of dogs and cats, but also more exotic ones like
dragons and chameleons.

The animals start out peaceful, but not tamed;
you have to tame them with with tripe rations
or scrolls of taming to make them your pets.

Prices would vary wildly; a little dog for $10,
or a gray dragon for $1000.

When you and your pet enter a pet shop, the shopkeeper
offers, "Sell your large dog? ($50?) (y/n?)"  If you
sell your dog, his little red heart goes away and
he's no longer "bonded" to you.

(Tricky point: would need some code to prevent
visiting pets from attacking pet-shop animals.)

(Tricky point: would need some code to limit
movement of pet-shop animals to within the
petshop.)

The shop also sells leashes, tripe rations,
whistles, magic whistles, stethescopes, potions of
healing (veternary medicine supplies), scrolls of
taming, etc.

To buy an animal, tame it.  "The zrutty devours a
tripe ration.  Buy a zrutty for $250? (y/n?)"  If
you say y, it's yours; otherwise, the little red
heart goes out again, and the zrutty reverts back
to pet-shop property.

(Tricky point: may need code to force all pet-shop
animals to find tripe rations irresistable.  Or
maybe not; perhaps force user to use other means
to tame "difficult" animals, such as reading a
scroll of taming near the animal.)


